try_err.wf:2:5: error: `try` needs a `catch` block
  |
2 |     try {
  |     ^^^
  = help: add `catch e { … }` after the `try` block
try_err.wf:6:5: error: `catch` without a matching `try`
  |
6 |     catch e { }
  |     ^^^^^
  = help: `catch` must follow the closing `}` of a `try` block
try_err.wf:7:5: error: `throw` needs an error value
  |
7 |     throw
  |     ^^^^^
  = help: write `throw e` to rethrow, or `throw error("message")`
try_err.wf:8:9: error: expected `{` to start the `try` body, found identifier `g`
  |
8 |     try g() catch e { }
  |         ^
  = help: braces are mandatory: `try … { … }`
